    "derivation": "Matched near-lossless CPL even mode line driven by SIN(0 1 312.5meg) through its own impedance: v(near)=0.5 sin(2 pi f t), v(far)=0.5 sin(2 pi f (t-Td)) for t>Td and 0 before, Td=8 ns = 2.5 periods, so v(far)=-v(near). The forced 1 ps step puts Td/1ps history points behind the far end, past the 2048-point capacity, and a curved waveform makes every drop the least-loss choice. Far-end atol 1e-3: the line model itself (ngspice's fit) sits up to 4.5e-4 V off the ideal delay.",
    "cross_check": "See the .sp header: ngspice-45 and ESPice 5275c0d3 on this netlist, and the planted cache bugs it catches.",
